# References, not resolved values. `npm run start:op` passes this file through
# `op inject` and exports the result only to the current Bash process, so no
# value is written into the working tree:
#
#     npm run start:op
#
# The script uses POSIX shell tools; on Windows run it from Git Bash or WSL, or
# follow the PowerShell instructions in docs/development.md.
#
# Both are EXPO_PUBLIC_, so they are compiled into the app bundle and are not
# secret from anyone holding the build. The client key is meant to be public —
# row-level security is what guards the data. This keeps resolved values out of
# git and gives maintainers one source of truth, nothing more.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=op://PressGolf/Supabase Project/url
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=op://PressGolf/Supabase Project/anon_key
